1
00:00:00,495 --> 00:00:05,237
Woodlands explores three garden communities for sixty homes in Lusaka,

2
00:00:05,454 --> 00:00:09,915
Zambia. The same brief sets a five-metre setback and a developed

3
00:00:09,929 --> 00:00:12,510
area below ten thousand square metres.

4
00:00:12,945 --> 00:00:17,470
We rotate the actual source model to
compare architectural relationships,

5
00:00:17,823 --> 00:00:21,097
rather than treating rendered imagery as a finished design.

6
00:00:22,842 --> 00:00:27,312
Four site readings connect location, access, amenities

7
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:28,793
and surrounding heights.

8
00:00:29,232 --> 00:00:34,327
The parcel sits within a connected
street network, near schools, services

9
00:00:34,422 --> 00:00:35,713
and open spaces.

10
00:00:36,148 --> 00:00:40,699
The height graphic describes mainly
one-to-two-storey housing, with smaller

11
00:00:40,713 --> 00:00:45,781
three-to-four-storey patches. Its tinted
areas and suggested height ranges

12
00:00:45,794 --> 00:00:49,096
are study interpretations, not a measured survey.

13
00:00:50,855 --> 00:00:54,918
The community ambition is clear: connected to the city, and at

14
00:00:54,931 --> 00:00:56,045
home in a garden.

15
00:00:56,471 --> 00:01:01,471
Three responses shape that ambition: a recognizable, quieter arrival;

16
00:01:01,783 --> 00:01:06,416
shared places for everyday encounters;
and homes benefiting from planting,

17
00:01:06,607 --> 00:01:07,789
outlook and privacy.

18
00:01:09,492 --> 00:01:14,139
Point Courtyard distributes four blocks around garden spaces, opening

19
00:01:14,152 --> 00:01:17,875
views while requiring careful spacing and repeated cores.

20
00:01:18,317 --> 00:01:22,420
Linear Terrace gives the site a clear
edge and connected outdoor setting,

21
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:25,993
with apartment depth and corridor daylight to resolve.

22
00:01:26,385 --> 00:01:30,910
Courtyard Block focuses shared life within a connected form; inner

23
00:01:30,923 --> 00:01:34,388
corners, overlooking and terrace boundaries need study.

24
00:01:36,091 --> 00:01:42,151
All three plans use the reported site area of 5,838.7

25
00:01:42,164 --> 00:01:47,444
square metres. Their overall totals are 9,748,

26
00:01:47,783 --> 00:01:52,580
9,622 and 9,658

27
00:01:52,593 --> 00:01:54,536
square metres, respectively.

28
00:01:54,927 --> 00:01:59,248
Derived floor-area ratios are approximately 1.39,

29
00:01:59,547 --> 00:02:05,280
1.37 and 1.38; footprint densities are 31.3,

30
00:02:05,552 --> 00:02:07,916
27 and 27 percent.

31
00:02:08,327 --> 00:02:10,297
These are concept estimates.

32
00:02:10,718 --> 00:02:14,563
Linear Terrace offers the most headroom below the brief limit.

33
00:02:14,971 --> 00:02:19,658
Each includes 1,620 square metres of reported basement

34
00:02:19,672 --> 00:02:24,441
parking: roughly thirty-five to forty-five spaces by area allowance,

35
00:02:24,713 --> 00:02:26,126
pending a real layout.

36
00:02:27,895 --> 00:02:32,420
The sections connect upper homes, lower amenities and shared outdoor

37
00:02:32,433 --> 00:02:37,057
life. Program colours, marker and pencil retain the same

38
00:02:37,071 --> 00:02:40,277
source cuts, while distant elements remain lighter.

39
00:02:40,685 --> 00:02:45,291
Missing interior partitions or structural details are not invented.

40
00:02:47,055 --> 00:02:51,552
Across all three options, five linked highlights identify residential

41
00:02:51,566 --> 00:02:56,009
space, amenities, landscape, water, and arrival.

42
00:02:56,448 --> 00:03:00,837
They reveal how homes meet gardens, pools and common routes.

43
00:03:01,244 --> 00:03:06,054
Every scheme links its five categories differently: open gaps in OP1,

44
00:03:06,326 --> 00:03:11,081
a continuous garden edge in OP2, and shared platforms in OP3.

45
00:03:11,516 --> 00:03:16,530
The coloured model and explanations remain
visible together; rotation supports

46
00:03:16,543 --> 00:03:20,619
spatial reading, and optional studio shadows clarify depth.

47
00:03:22,362 --> 00:03:24,957
Three references sharpen the questions.

48
00:03:25,369 --> 00:03:29,866
Berlin’s OASIS suggests garden spaces between separate homes.

49
00:03:30,257 --> 00:03:34,931
TOMAZ in Porto Alegre connects residential edges with planting and

50
00:03:34,944 --> 00:03:39,441
shared leisure. Guadalajara’s La Toscana organizes common

51
00:03:39,455 --> 00:03:40,950
ground and terraces.

52
00:03:41,374 --> 00:03:46,102
These are lessons to adapt locally, not designs or performance results

53
00:03:46,116 --> 00:03:46,768
to copy.

54
00:03:48,491 --> 00:03:52,635
Comparison combines reported areas with spatial judgments.

55
00:03:53,064 --> 00:03:57,602
Linear Terrace has the greatest area allowance; Point Courtyard has

56
00:03:57,616 --> 00:03:59,463
the largest residential area.

57
00:03:59,871 --> 00:04:04,599
Priority sliders explore garden life, context, privacy,

58
00:04:04,885 --> 00:04:06,556
simplicity and headroom.

59
00:04:06,963 --> 00:04:12,031
Changing those priorities changes the
ranking: it remains a concept assessment,

60
00:04:12,262 --> 00:04:13,675
not objective proof.

61
00:04:15,455 --> 00:04:19,667
The seventeen original pages remain available, from the brief and site

62
00:04:19,681 --> 00:04:24,626
analyses to sketches, plans, model views, function diagrams

63
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:29,617
and comparison. This montage preserves the source evidence alongside

64
00:04:29,631 --> 00:04:31,519
the interactive interpretation.

65
00:04:33,788 --> 00:04:37,619
The next choice is which relationships to develop and test.

66
00:04:38,059 --> 00:04:42,841
Dwelling plans, access, daylight, privacy, landscape,

67
00:04:43,086 --> 00:04:45,980
structure and parking will determine their quality.

68
00:04:46,415 --> 00:04:50,925
The interactive book keeps the three
alternatives, their evidence and their

69
00:04:50,939 --> 00:04:53,738
unresolved questions available for that work.
